   "he": "״עַד שֶׁיַּעֲבוֹר הַקַּיִץ״, עַד שֶׁיִּכָּפְלוּ הַמַּקְצוּעוֹת. תָּנָא: עַד שֶׁיַּכְפִּילוּ רוֹב הַמַּקְצוּעוֹת.",
   "en": "§ The mishna states that if one said: «Until the summer has passed,» then the vow remains in effect «until» the people «set aside the knives» used to cut the figs. It was «taught:» This means «until most» people «set aside» their «knives,» even if there are still some individuals who have yet to do so."
